{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Jacob vowed a vow.</b> And if you ask: but we say — better than this is one who does not vow at all. One may answer, <b>לאמר</b> is written, to teach the generations that they should vow in a time of their distress, just as he vowed in a time of trouble." "<b>If Elohim will be with me.</b> He was fearful lest sin cause [the promise to be voided]. And some interpret it in the language of an oath, that is: thus <b>may Elohim be with me and keep me on the way</b>, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:31.163896366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}